! Test v1.09.2 (2/2): always-on point-group detection and the
! post-optimization re-detection / change notice.
! A deliberately distorted water seed (Cs -- any triatomic is at
! least planar) optimizes back toward the C2v minimum; with the
! LOOSened %symmetry_tol below, the optimizer's residual asymmetry
! (~1e-2 bohr at the default convergence thresholds) falls inside
! the detection tolerance and the group change is reported:
!   startup:  "Point group: Cs"
!   post-opt: "Point group after optimization: C2v  (was Cs)"
! With the default %symmetry_tol (1e-3 bohr) the same run honestly
! reports Cs (unchanged): recovering the EXACT group needs the
! residual asymmetry below the tolerance.  The re-detection itself
! runs for EVERY optimization job, with no keyword required.
%method  HF
%basis   sto-3g
%job     opt
%symmetry_tol 0.08
*geometry angstrom
 O   0.000000    0.000000    0.121300
 H   0.000000    0.900000   -0.429200
 H   0.000000   -0.620000   -0.489200
*end
